The original calls the virtual `GetType()` up to twice per invocation. This version calls it once and reuses the result. That saves one virtual dispatch on a hot path. Behavior is unchanged, assuming `GetType()` has no side effects, which is expected for a const getter.

```cpp
FIT_UINT8 FieldBase::GetNumValues(void) const
{
    if (!IsValid())
        return 0;

    const FIT_UINT8 type = GetType();
    if (type != FIT_BASE_TYPE_STRING)
        return (FIT_UINT8)(values.size() / baseTypeSizes[type & FIT_BASE_TYPE_NUM_MASK]);

    return (FIT_UINT8)stringIndexes.size();
}
```